    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="II As. Inscr." corresp="#wit-h">Æþelstanes gerænesse.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">Æþelstanes gerædnesse.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">Æthelstan's ordinances.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Aethelstans Gesetze. H)</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Æthelstan's laws. H)</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Heading only in H (in red), after Walreaf; Liebermann would correct to ‘gerædn.’. B has no heading, so K is empty. Base text B = CCCC 383 (c. 1130); H = Textus Roffensis; Ot = Cotton Otho B XI (burnt; here mostly known from Somner's transcript, So).</note>
      </div>
    </body>
